Every morning, Bella would 43 Tom to the bus stop for his commute to work. She knew exactly when to stop at street crossings and how to 44 obstacles on the sidewalk. Tom trusted Bella completely. "She's not just a pet," Tom often said. "She's my 45."

One rainy evening, as they were walking home, Bella suddenly 46 in her tracks. Tom felt the pull on the harness and stopped immediately. 47 he could react, he heard a loud crash — a car had run a red light and 48 right where they would have been walking.

Tom knelt down and hugged Bella tightly. "You 49 my life," he whispered. The story made headlines, and Bella was 50 a local hero award by the city mayor.

After Bella retired at age 10, Tom got a new guide dog named Max. But Bella stayed with the family as a beloved 51. She spent her retirement 52 on the couch, playing in the garden, and 53 receiving extra treats from Tom's children.

"Bella taught me that love has no 54," Tom says. "She saw the world for me when I couldn't, and I will be 55 grateful for that."

**第41题:** A. blind  B. deaf  C. elderly  D. disabled
**答案:** A（导盲犬帮助盲人）

**第42题:** A. waited for  B. looked after  C. played with  D. searched for
**答案:** B（照顾主人）

**第43题:** A. drive  B. push  C. guide  D. carry
**答案:** C（guide dog 引导）

